From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 15:02:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 510/510] [DS4.1] mHC finalize writes its output's MXFP8 cast;
 the projections it feeds stop casting

Every TileLang decode layer cast the same BF16 rows three times with
TileKernels' per_token_cast: the attention entry's output for the fused
Q-A/KV projection, and the FFN entry's output twice, for the shared expert's
gate/up and for the routed experts. mHC finalize holds those rows in
registers when it writes them, so it now writes their cast in the same
launch: per 32 columns (four adjacent lanes, two lane shuffles for the
block's amax) the E4M3 bytes and the UE8M0 byte, by _reference_cast's
arithmetic (gemm.cast_block_mxfp8), which is per_token_cast's byte for byte.

The entry returns the cast as a sixth output (linear.MXFP8Rows, padded to
whole decode tiles)
and the decoder layer hands it to the sublayer for the call
(kernels.mxfp8_inputs). The projections it feeds are marked
tilelang_mxfp8_input and cast nothing: one that gets no cast, or another
tensor's, fails rather than casting; a split-K projection cannot be marked.
The routed experts read it the same way (TileLangExperts, plan.run takes
MXFP8Rows), and their workspace loses the tokens' copy.

Rows regrouped after the entry are cast once by per_token_cast
(linear.cast_mxfp8): a CED boundary's compact rows, and prefill SP's
gathered rows (attention's with a compressor, and the FFN's, which the
release cast twice). The decoder layer declares that cast (_warm_casts);
the MoE plan no longer warms one.

Ceiling (c1 decode profile, inventory 5): about 0.5% at c1 for the entries'
casts, of 1.3% for every per_token_cast launch.

Tests: every entry test also checks the cast against per_token_cast of the
y it wrote, plus scale regimes (zero, below the 1e-4 floor, above 448,
powers of two), both finalize widths, a NaN token and the regrouped rows'
cast; a marked projection gives the self-casting one's bits at decode and
prefill sizes and fails without its cast; the MoE tests hand the plan its
MXFP8 rows. Benchmark (gated): finalize with the cast against the release's
finalize and the casts it replaces, decode entries and an SP prefill layer.
